  "notes": "Source: official Baylor School of Engineering & Computer Science flowchart 'COMPUTER SCIENCE MAJOR (CS Concentration) (2026-2027)' (https://web.ecs.baylor.edu/flowchart/flowcharts/bscs-cs.pdf, revised 4/25 SEM). The CS Concentration is the general track of Baylor's Bachelor of Science in Computer Science (B.S.C.S.); the Software and Cybersecurity concentrations publish their own separate flowcharts and were NOT used. Course titles, credit hours, and prerequisites were cross-checked against the official Baylor Undergraduate Catalog course-description pages (catalog.baylor.edu/undergraduate/courses-instruction/csi/ and the ECS program requirement tables). Transcription method: flowchart PDF downloaded from Baylor ECS, rendered to a high-resolution image, and transcribed term by term; every term's hours were re-summed to match the flowchart's published term totals (16/16/15/16/16/15/15/15 = 124). Caveats: (1) CSI 3351 'Foundations of AI' is new for 2026-2027 and not yet listed on the catalog CSI course-description page; its title, 3 credits, and prerequisite (CSI 3336, solid prereq arrow on the flowchart, verified by zooming the rendered image) come from the official flowchart. (2) CHA 10XX Chapel is required for two semesters at 0 credits each per the catalog ('Chapel: Two Semesters | 0'); the same official code appears twice, both flagged required_zero. (3) Courses marked with beta on the flowchart (CSI 1430, CSI 1440) must be completed with a grade of B or better; a C or better is required in all major courses and math prerequisites. (4) CSI 43C9 Capstone Design Project additionally requires senior standing, which is not encodable as a course prerequisite. (5) Science requirement per the flowchart: one 8-hour group (BIO 1305/1105 + 1306/1106, CHE 1301/1101 + 1302/1102, GEO 1305/1105 + 1306/1106, or PHY 1408 + 1409 / PHY 1420 + 1430) plus six to eight additional hours; the flowchart places four 4-hour SCIENCE slots (Fall Y1, Fall Y3, Spring Y3, Fall Y4). (6) Foreign Language & Culture is 3 hours from the ECS distribution list in the Undergraduate Catalog (flowchart '*' note). (7) English Literature slot: ENG 2310, Foreign Literature, or Literature in Context distribution list (flowchart star note). (8) Contemporary Social Issues: one 3-hour course from the corresponding A&S distribution list (HIS 1300 included). ENCODING: second Chapel coded \"CHA 10XX-2\" (title preserved) because the pipeline rejects duplicate course codes; the catalog requires the same 0-credit CHA 10XX in two semesters.",
